        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.00053/2611.00053v1/TeaserFig__41_.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:(Left)SIMIT. Given an unlabeled test query1, the VLM imagines similar samples2, uses them to improve itself via in-context learning or by fine-tuning3, and answers the original test query with the self-improved model4. No labels or external models are used.(Right)Mean relative gain versus runtime across 17 benchmarks.",
                "position": 260
            }
        ]
    },
