        "header": "2Related Work",
        "images": []
    },
    {
        "header": "3Methods",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.00053/2611.00053v1/MainPipelineFig__26_.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:SIMIT’s synthetic data generation pipeline.\nGiven an unlabeled test query, the model allocates a synthesis budget\nand proposes diverse question-answer pairs with corresponding image\ndescriptions. Answers are fixed before images are realized through\nnative generation or rendering skills. Verification and difficulty\nfiltering retain accurate and informative examples.The same model serves as the synthesizer, router, critic, and solver.This figure shows only the data synthesis stage.\nBut the model then self-improves with the final samples via in-context learning or finetuning.",
                "position": 385
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.00053/2611.00053v1/ImageGenerationSamples__4_.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Representative visuals synthesized by SIMIT.\nCombining native image generation with rendering skills enables\nBAGEL-7B to produce natural images, structured visuals, and\ncomposite layouts within a single pipeline.\nCorresponding generation prompts are in\nAppendixG.4.",
                "position": 466
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "header": "4Experiments",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.00053/2611.00053v1/QualitativeSamplesEval__14_.png",
                "caption": "Figure 4:Each method’s retrieved/generated\ndemonstrations and final answers for two test queries. Nearest real neighbors can be off-topic, and TTT-NN sometimes inherits that mismatch. SIMIT’s demonstrations match the query’s subject, and both its variants answer correctly.\nSee AppendixNfor more qualitative samples. Retrieval-based methods are bottlenecked by\ndataset coverage. Self-generated demos, targeted to the query,\nrecover from it without requiring annotated retrieval sets.",
                "position": 1183
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.00053/2611.00053v1/SamplesSkillLibraryAblation_Horizontal__2_.png",
                "caption": "Figure 5:Generations with and without our skill library. BAGEL cannot draw structured visuals, and often fails to generate legible text.",
                "position": 1658
            }
        ]
    },
